s raised over the capital the  survivor's flag is dedicated to the  countless indigenous people who endured  the agony of residential schools and  it's going to fly over parliament hill  for the next two years before being  moved to a permanent home karen  lieberman has more  a symbol of a history once rooted in  shame now rising above parliament hill  it's a reminder that the survivors in  this country  are not to be forgotten the prime  minister joining indigenous canadians  from across the country to raise the  survivor's flag honoring those who were  forced into canada's residential school  system take an opportunity to meet us  know who we are don't just talk about us  don't own us as our survivors the orange  and white flag was designed by the  national center for truth and  reconciliation each element like the  children taken from their families and  the eagle feather all symbolically  significant and carefully selected in  consultation with survivors  you can see that the strength and the  commitment in the flag itself  and you can see their hope for the  future  the hope that the seeds that rest  beneath the soil will someday sprout and  bloom again as prophesied by our people  it says that we acknowledge  the intergenerational  trauma these  so-called schools  have caused  and that we  commit to continue working together  towards a future of healing  and partnership  last month a long-awaited public apology  on canadian soil by pope francis  sorry for the ways in which regrettably  for the church's role in  government-funded schools meant to  destroy indigenous culture and language  saint hen's residential school survivor  evelyn corkmas met with the pope and  previously traveled to rome and i  presented him with an empty box and i  asked him this is where i want you to  put the residential school documents  more than the symbolic gesture of a flag  cork mask wants all documents related to  residential schools released  it opens the true history of canada 